Description: PowerToys-style utilities for Ubuntu
 Knobu adds small power tools to the desktop, each one a module that can be
 switched on or off in the Knobu settings app:
 .
  * Command Bar: floating launcher (Alt+Space), app search, calculator, unit
    and currency converter, emoji picker, window switcher, and OS shortcut override.
  * Clipboard History: floating searchable clipboard palette (Super+V), image
    clip thumbnails, URL tracking parameter sanitization, and SQLite storage.
  * Touchpad Gestures: slide three fingers to change the volume, tap to mute
    or to play and pause media.
  * Keyboard Manager: remap keys and shortcuts on every keyboard, in every
    app, on Wayland and X11.
  * Awake: keep the computer and screen awake without changing power
    settings.
  * Color Picker: pick a colour from anywhere on screen and copy it as HEX,
    RGB or HSL.
  * Text Extractor: select an area of the screen and copy the text in it.
 .
 Fully supported on Kubuntu (KDE Plasma 6); Ubuntu (GNOME) support is in
 beta. Reading the touchpad and keyboards requires membership of the "input"
 group. The package installs a udev rule that lets members of that group
 create virtual keyboards, which Keyboard Manager needs.
